ine.html">Contact</a></nav></header><main class="wrap section"><div class="eyebrow">Black File · Public Records</div><h1>EPSTEIN FILE CHECK.</h1><p class="lead">Search, submit, classify and route Epstein-related public files into an evidence ledger, review queue, missing-record tracker, Matrix card links, cautious conclusions and Theory Lab.</p><section class="section ep-card sensitive"><h2>Evidence Boundary</h2><p>Appearance in an Epstein-related public file is a research lead, not proof of wrongdoing. This system separates documented fact, sourced analysis, reasonable inference, speculation, unsupported claims, and missing records. No person, company, institution, flight, address, meeting, email, phone number, or association should be treated as proof of serious conduct unless supported by court records, sworn evidence, official findings, judgments, or other reliable public records.</p></section><div class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href="epstein-search.html">Search</a><a class="btn alt" href="epstein-upload-check.html">Submit File</a><a class="btn alt" href="epstein-evidence-boundary.html">Evidence Boundary</a><a class="btn alt" href="epstein-theory-lab.html">Theory Lab</a></div><section class="section"><h2>System Flow</h2><div class="ep-grid"><article class="ep-card"><h3>Ingest</h3><p>Accept public source URL, pasted text or placeholder upload.</p></article><article class="ep-card"><h3>Extract</h3><p>OCR and entity extraction placeholder.</p></article><article class="ep-card"><h3>Classify</h3><p>Assign evidence level and confidence.</p></article><article class="ep-card"><h3>Route</h3><p>Suggest cards, dossiers, source ledger and missing records.</p></article><article class="ep-card"><h3>Review</h3><p>Legal-sensitive, unclear or weak items stay in review.</p></article><article class="ep-card"><h3>Publish</h3><p>Only evidence-bounded conclusions are published.</p></article></div></section><!-- cinematic-pathways:start --><section class="matrix-pathways" aria-labelle